bevy-horizon: NAK_DEBUG=ubra, plain branches for uniform ifs before Volta

For mesa-switch (https://github.com/danfromtico/mesa-switch, by danfromtico and NaGaa95; MIT)
at d4a00ea0ab3f59afb967cc5d779e4263d237bd77, after 0001 to 0005. scripts/build_nvk.sh applies
it; this text before the first "diff --git" line is ignored by git apply.

Before SM70, from_nir.rs puts an SSY before every if and a SYNC at the end of each side, so the
warp's threads come back together after it. A warp whose threads all take the same side never
splits, so there is nothing to bring back together. nak_nir.c runs NIR's divergence analysis
for every SM, and from SM70 nak_nir_lower_cf uses it to give such ifs plain branches.
NAK_DEBUG=ubra does the same before SM70: an if whose condition is not divergent gets a
predicated BRA and no SSY or SYNC. Loops keep their PBK and PCNT.

On Skate 3's world fragment shader (SM53, with xbar,sink,remat and the game's bounds checks),
NAK_DEBUG=stats went from 3570 instructions to 3558 (static cycles 22261 to 22200), and with
SKATE_WORLD_PAGE_ARRAY from 2295 to 2283. Bevy 0.18.1's PBR fragment shader went from 2679 to
2649. No shader failed to compile on the PC (nakhost, SM53, debug build with assertions). Not
yet run on hardware; off unless set.

